    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 615,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Ihy\nIhy is a god in ancient Egyptian mythology who represents the ecstasy of playing the sistrum . His name may mean `` sistrum player '' , referring to his function , or `` calf '' . This is in allusion to his relationship with the cow goddess Hathor who was often said to be his mother . Other goddesses might be called his mother , however , including Isis , Sekhmet , and Neith . The god Horus is Ihy 's father . Ihy was depicted as a child holding a sistrum or as a nude child with his finger in his mouth . He was worshiped alongside Horus and Hathor at Dendera . Hathor was his mother and Horus as his father"
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
